335: *** AND THE FACE THIS DETECTOR DID **NOT** CLOSE UNTIL REPAIR 15, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE A CONTRACT THAT
336:     HIDES ITS HOLES IS WORSE THAN NONE. ***
337:   THE DECLINE-SUPPRESSION FACE.  The `goto crime_declined' SKIPS the register switch, and what it skips is
338:   an OMISSION -- it reads, writes and tests nothing -- so every floor clause in this project enumerates the
339:   EMPTY SET over it.  Two mutants that condition the `goto' on a LABEL score 188/188 against this probe:  [188-row]
340:       M3_timelatch   the goto moved inside the latch block, exempting CRIME_TIME  -- 188/188  [188-row]
341:       M5_revlatch    the same at CRIME_REV                                        -- 188/188  [188-row]
342:   with M4_timeplain (the same edit WITHOUT the latch conjunct) killed at 184/188 and M6_istlatch (the same  [188-row]
343:   edit at INTSTAT) killed at 185/188 -- the controls that make those two escapes mean `no row looked'.  [188-row]
344:   *** REPAIR 15 (2026-09-26) ROWS THE OPEN CELLS.  The floor, by the flagship's first-hand re-ruling
345:   (artifacts/crimewidthkill/rerule_20260925/fable5_rerule_529_20260925.md), is {observable skipped label} x
346:   {latch SET}.  M3/M5 escaped because no refusal at TIME or REV with the latch already SET had a channel: the
347:   `time' and `rev' sessions refuse there FIRST, and the `latch x5' session's later refusals at +0x00 and +0x38
348:   run from CODE (REV's redirect needs the PROM window) with no TIME sample after them.  The `tl' and `rl' rows
349:   refuse at +0x07 FIRST, then at the label.  The five guest-observable labels, the label-swap built for each,
350:   and the table that measures it (scores are in those tables' logs, never here):
351:       INTSTAT  M6_istlatch      istat sb/lh/sh                  repair14_20260916/ (table 12)
352:       INTMASK  M7_intmasklatch  imask sb/lh/sh                  table13a_20260925/
353:       CONTROL  M8_ctllatch      sb08 msg, sh08b run, gate run   table13a_20260925/
354:       TIME     M3_timelatch     tl lb/sb/lh/sh                  table14_20260926/
355:       REV      M5_revlatch      rl lb/lh/sb/sh pc               table14_20260926/
356:   DOG (a bare `break;') and default (host log only -- and `mid nodflt' already reads it after a latch-
357:   setting refusal: M1_gotolatch reddened it in table 12) have no guest-observable arm: clause (e).
358:   ENTRIES 13 AND 17 of ACCEPTS (`sw'/`sd +0x08 = 0x0200', CONTROL's DOG mask): the arm clears DOG and nothing
359:   prints, and the prelude re-forces the register at every access, so the CONTROL text COUNT is the cell's one
360:   observable -- and no row read it in a session holding that write.  `ctldog sw msg'/`ctldog sd msg' are the pair
361:   (D_nodogclear, the DOG branch's clear deleted; table14_20260926/).  A SILENT decline of the DOG-only write
362:   changes nothing any access can see: EQUIVALENT, disclosed.
363:   REPAIR 16 (2026-09-26) PINS THE CONTROL ARM'S RESIDUE-TEXT COUNT FOR EACH OF ITS THREE CLEARS IN BOTH LATCH
364:   STATES.  FLOOR: the two TESTED bits' clears (DOG, HARD_RESET -- each masked as a case in the arm), in the
365:   latch-CLEAR state where an accepted write's residue is the cell's only observable -- the CHANNEL conditional on
366:   entries 13 and 17 (rerule_20260925/), extended by sibling parity to the arm's other tested bit
367:   (repair15_pass2_20260926/fable5_r15p2.md): `ctldog sw/sd msg' (D_nodogclear), `ctlrst sw/sd msg' (H_noresetclear).
368:   Everything else in this block is a STRENGTHENING above that floor, measured in table15a_20260926/ and
369:   table16_20260926/.
370:   THE LATCH IS NOT AN AXIS OF THIS ARM: the CONTROL arm reads no latch (`d->warned' has one reader and one writer,
371:   both in the decline block), so a clear gated on it is clause (e) -- ROWED ANYWAY: `rearm ctl msg' (DOG, latch
372:   SET; L_dogclr) and `rst 4w/8w msg' (HARD_RESET, latch SET; L_rstclr).
373:   ENDIANESS (0x0100) is cleared unconditionally and never branched on: clause (e), NOT a member of the tested-bit
374:   class.  Its clear skipped (E_noendianclear) is carried as a SIDE EFFECT of the ten-write aggregate counts, a
375:   strengthening and not a floor claim.
376:   `latch ctl msg' (CLEAR) and `rearm ctl msg' (SET) are AGGREGATE prefix counts over the ten accepted CONTROL
377:   writes in ACCEPTS (every `rearm' entry runs latch SET: the refused `lb +0x07' precedes the loop).  They attribute
378:   by count value only -- L_dogclr and an ENDIANESS-latch-SET skip both read 6 on `rearm'; W_ctl8w reads 2 -- and
