381:   is set -- a floor cell crossed with one bit of the relationally compared residue (#549 D1) -- leaves every count
382:   unchanged: MEASURED for DOG (D_dogbit0: the 0x0201 twin prints 0x201 where the fix prints 0x1); DERIVED, not
383:   built, for HARD_RESET and ENDIANESS (every accepted reset store here is exactly 0x0800; both 0x0100 writes have
384:   bit 0 clear).  Clause (e), disclosed as a family.  A value anchor BESIDE the prefix count would carry the DOG
385:   instance at zero sessions (filed); an anchor IN PLACE of it loses H_noresetclear (the `ctlrst' twin 0x0001 carries
386:   no HARD_RESET bit: repair16_f2_20260926/opus_f2/replay_ctl.out).
