473:     clamp of an access straddling a device's end (`len = mem->devices[i].length - paddr;') cannot make one here only
474:     because DEV_CRIME_LENGTH is 0x280, a multiple of 8 -- one `#define' away from false (filed: `crimesplitwidth').
475:     The unaligned-pair instructions (lwl/lwr/swl/swr, ldl/ldr) are not rowed.  The RAM-size checks ABOVE the width
476:     arm (`-M 48' exits at the first CRIME access) are filed, not here.
477:   * a TRANSLATION of the register decode -- every access landing some whole number of registers away, +1, +2 or
478:     more, either direction: no table built one, so none is a measured claim here.  The ANCHORED rows (`top8 anchor',
479:     `top4 anchor': a value the prelude writes by bank index, not through the decode under test) are placed to see
480:     one; that is a reading, not a measurement (clause (f); the 09-25 re-ruling, as GPT-6 Astra confirmed it).
481:   * independence between two CRIME instances (the latch is per instance by construction; IP32 has one CRIME).
482:   * bits the CONTROL arm neither tests nor clears (SOFT_RESET 0x0400, the SYSADC bits, the low nibbles) are written
483:     by no accepted row; an edit keyed on one is outside this contract (repair 16's F2 adjudication, X7).
484: 
485: Sentinel: CRIMEP_DONE (plus CRIMEP_RESULT=n/N and CRIMEP_CONTROL=OK|FAIL).
486: """
487: import os, pty, re, select, signal, sys, time
488: 
489: BIN = sys.argv[1]
490: LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"
491: DUMMY = "/tmp/dummy_crimep.bin"
492: if not os.path.exists(DUMMY):
493:     with open(DUMMY, "wb") as f:
494:         f.write(b"\0" * 16)
495: 
496: CODE = 0x80001000
497: SCRATCH_RAM = 0xa0001800
498: LIVE_VAL = 0x12345678
499: CRIME = 0xb4000000
500: SENT = 0xdeadbeef
501: RA = 0x80004000
502: PROBE_PC = 0xbfc05180           # inside the CRIME_REV hack's window, (pc & 0xffffff00) == 0xbfc05100
503: 
504: R = {"zero": 0, "at": 1, "v0": 2, "v1": 3, "a0": 4, "a1": 5, "a2": 6, "a3": 7, "t0": 8, "t1": 9,
505:      "s0": 16, "s1": 17, "s2": 18, "s3": 19, "s4": 20, "ra": 31}
506: OPC = {"lb": 0x20, "lh": 0x21, "lw": 0x23, "lbu": 0x24, "lhu": 0x25, "ld": 0x37,
507:        "sb": 0x28, "sh": 0x29, "sw": 0x2b, "sd": 0x3f}
508: OP_B_SELF = 0x1000ffff
509: OP_NOP = 0
510: 
511: 
512: def enc(op, rs, rt, imm=0):
513:     return (OPC[op] << 26) | (R[rs] << 21) | (R[rt] << 16) | (imm & 0xffff)
514: 
515: 
516: #  hand-assembled encodings checked against the committed witness's constants (a wrong register field reads 0, which
517: #  a decline's own answer would accept by accident -- so the accept rows carry nonzero wants)
518: assert enc("lb", "at", "v0") == 0x80220000 and enc("lhu", "at", "v0") == 0x94220000
519: assert enc("sb", "a3", "t0") == 0xa0e80000 and enc("sh", "a3", "t0") == 0xa4e80000
520: assert enc("sw", "a3", "t0") == 0xace80000 and enc("lw", "at", "v0") == 0x8c220000
