29:     reds  imask sb   CHANNEL: cause IP2 printed after `sb +0x18 0xff' -- the arm reasserts with INTMASK = SOFTINT = BIT
30:                      (stored by the two accepted sd), so IP2 goes SET; the row wants clear.
31:           imask lh   same channel, the next `print cause' (IP2 stays set: nothing deasserts it).
32:           imask sh   same channel, the next `print cause'.
33:     green imask pre / imask lb (lb +0x18 is the session's FIRST refusal: declined, latch set) / imask ctl (wants set) /
34:           imask once, said (one announce) / imask lb v0, lh v0 (the width arm is skipped either way: answers 0) /
35:           imask keeps (no store lands: INTMASK stays BIT).  The istat session refuses at 0x10 only: unaffected.
