39:     reds  sb08 msg   CHANNEL: the CONTROL arm's `unimplemented control' text.  `sb 0x01' is the first refusal (declined);
40:                      `sb 0xff' falls through with idata 0xff: no DOG, no RESET, ENDIANESS clear -> 0xff != 0 -> fatal().
41:           sh08b run  CHANNEL: the RAM trip's v1.  `sh 0x0201' first (declined); `sh 0x0900' falls through with
42:                      HARD_RESET (0x800) set -> every CPU's running = 0 -> the roundtrip never runs.
43:           gate run   CHANNEL: v1.  `lb +0x08' first (declined); `lh +0x08' falls through as a READ (the arm does nothing
44:                      on reads: answers 0, green); `sh 0x0800' falls through with HARD_RESET -> CPUs stop.
45:     possible  gate lb v0 / gate lh v0: their `print t1' / `print s3' come AFTER the stopping store; if the emulator
46:                      ends when every CPU stops, the prints never happen and both read absent (red).  Not predicted
47:                      either way -- it depends on what the debugger does with no running CPU, which I have not read.
48:     green sh08 run/pc (`sh 0x0800' is that session's FIRST refusal: declined) / sb08 run (0xff stops nothing) /
49:           sh08b msg (0x0900 is cleared to 0 by the arm; the 0xffff store never runs once the CPUs stop) /
50:           sh08b once, said / dog-session ctl v0, ctl lb v0 (READS at +0x08: the arm does nothing on a read; answers 0).
51:     Score: at most 201/204 (three certain reds), at least 199/204.
