6: WHY.  Repair 15's pass 2 (repair15_pass2_20260926/) found the CONTROL arm's residue-text channel covered for one clear
7: in one latch state only.  The dedicated grok seat found H_noresetclear (the HARD_RESET branch's clear skipped: an
8: accepted 0x800 write also prints, and no row counted it); the Fable seat graded it L2, like the DOG pair; table 15a
9: measured it at 218/218.  The Opus measuring seat measured the same channel's other open cells (the DOG clear skipped
10: with the latch SET; the ENDIANESS clear) and proposed CONTROL-text counts on the two existing ACCEPTS sessions.  Two
11: consecutive passes in one class, so repair 16 closes the class in one diff: every clear the arm makes before its
12: residue test, in both latch states.
13: 
14: INSTRUMENT: crime_width_probe.table16.py = mk_r16.py (beside this file) applied to repair 15's probe f5e915f6; md5
15: 5f770991.  226 rows = 218 + 8:
16:     ctlrst sw msg / sd msg         NEW session per width: 0x0001 then 0x0800 at +0x08, latch CLEAR; CONTROL-text count 1
17:     ctlrst sw halt / sd halt       the same sessions' RAM trip: v1 at the sentinel (the 0x0800 write reached the arm)
18:     rst 4w msg / rst 8w msg        the EXISTING reset sessions, now with a 0x0001 twin first: CONTROL-text count 1
19:     rearm ctl msg                  the EXISTING re-arm session's CONTROL-text count, 4 (ten ACCEPTS writes, latch SET)
20:     latch ctl msg                  the EXISTING latch session's CONTROL-text count, 4 (the same ten, latch CLEAR)
21: plus text: the header's {1,2} x {R,W} claim scoped to "at least one latch state", the contract's class closure and its
22: list of cells NOT rowed, the tl/rl rationale.  Every other session is repair 15's, unchanged; the reset sessions gain
23: one accepted store before their refusal.
24: BASELINE: dev_sgi_ip32.c 8c1d1545 (unchanged since table 12); clone /tmp/gxopus_r14, restored cmp-clean with a fresh
25: binary after table 15a, no .MUTANT.  The driver rebuilds base IN THE CLONE and checks [ binary -nt source ].
26: 
