81:   GUARD vs BODY   The new mutants' guards read len and d->warned, which the CONTROL arm's body never reads;
82:                   d->warned has ONE writer (the decline block).
83:   CHANNEL         Per new row, above; check16.py scores each named channel under each named mutant.
84:   ROW-LIST DIFF   The Fable seat prescribed `ctlrst sw/sd msg' with the halt as liveness: present.  The Opus seat's two
85:                   options: the ACCEPTS-session counts are present; the residue-VALUE text is not rowed (disclosed).
