16:     len2only  38/40  CONTROL=OK   goto only for len 2 (1-byte cells fall in)
17:     readonly  37/40  CONTROL=OK   goto only for reads (write cells fall in)
18:     wronly    38/40  CONTROL=OK   goto only for writes (read cells fall in)
19:     return1   40/40  CONTROL=OK   PREDICTED EQUIVALENT, measured equivalent (memory_rw pre-zero, #95) -- disclosed
20:     nolatch   39/40  CONTROL=OK   latch never set
21:     latchinv  35/40  CONTROL=OK   latch test inverted
22:     fmtswap   36/40  CONTROL=OK   announce's len/addr swapped
23:     acc8w     36/40  CONTROL=OK   8W refused
24:     acc8r     37/40  CONTROL=OK   8R refused
25:     acc4wlo   38/40  CONTROL=OK   4W low half refused
26:     acc4whi   37/40  CONTROL=FAIL 4W high half refused
27:     acc4rlo   38/40  CONTROL=FAIL 4R low half refused
28:     acc4rhi   38/40  CONTROL=FAIL 4R high half refused
29:   17 of 17 non-equivalent mutants KILLED; the one equivalent (return1) is the one predicted.
30:   *** CORRECTED 2026-09-13 (pass 2: codex, grok, glm, kimi CLI and kimi-k3:cloud, independently): this line read
31:   "18 of 18 non-equivalent mutants KILLED".  The table is base + 18 mutants; return1 is one of the 18 and is
32:   equivalent, so 17 are non-equivalent.  It counted return1 as both equivalent and killed. ***
33: 
34: ROWS EACH MUTANT REDDENED vs PRETABLE section 4
35:     revert    all 29 refusal rows                                                        = predicted
36:     fault     <op> v0/pc/exc x (lb lh lbu lhu sb sh) + sh08 pc + lb/lh rev pc (pc at the vector)   = predicted (+ the
37:               pc-only rows of the side-effect sessions, which see the vector too)
38:     exit0     every surv/v0/pc/exc row + sh08 pc/run + rev pc + latch surv; <op> said and latch x5 GREEN
39:               (announce printed, EOF, status 0)                                          = predicted
40:     fallsw    sh08 pc, sh08 run, sb08 msg, lb rev pc, lh rev pc                          = predicted, exactly
41:     len1only  sh08 pc, sh08 run, lh rev pc                                               = predicted, exactly
42:     len2only  sb08 msg, lb rev pc                                                        = predicted, exactly
43:     readonly  sh08 pc, sh08 run, sb08 msg                                                = predicted, exactly
44:     wronly    lb rev pc, lh rev pc                                                       = predicted, exactly
45:     nolatch   latch x5                                                                   = predicted
46:     latchinv  <op> said x4, latch x5                                                     = predicted
47:     fmtswap   <op> said x4                                                               = predicted
48:     acc8r     acc8 st+ld, acc4 wlo, acc4 whi                                             = predicted
49:     acc4wlo   acc4 wlo, acc4 whi                                                         = predicted
50:     acc4whi   acc4 whi  + controls sw08 halts, sw08 msg ctl                              see (b)
51:     acc4rlo   acc4 rlo  + control devsig                                                 see (b)
52:     acc4rhi   acc4 rhi  + control rev pc ctl                                             see (b)
53:     acc8w     acc8 st+ld, acc4 rhi, acc4 rlo, acc4 wlo                                   *** PREDICTION WRONG, see (a)
54: 
55: (a) THE CHANNEL LINE'S OWN CLAIM, checked as PRETABLE promised.  "A row's channel under its mutant is knowable at
56:     writing time" held for 16 of 17 non-equivalent mutants, ROW SET EXACT (this said "17 of 18", the same miscount).  For acc8w I predicted {acc8, rhi, wlo,
57:     whi} and measured {acc8, rhi, RLO, wlo}: the accept session is SEQUENTIAL, so with the sd refused the register
58:     stays 0, the lw of the low half reads 0 (rlo red -- I had missed it), and the later sw of the high half on top of
59:     the earlier sw of the low half REBUILDS the full word the whi row wants (whi green -- I had predicted it red).
60:     The kill is unaffected (four rows), and every accept cell still reds under its OWN single-cell mutant.  The
61:     lesson is narrow and real: in a session where later accesses write the same register, a row's value depends on
62:     every earlier access, so its channel under a mutant must be traced through the whole sequence, not read off the
63:     one access it names.
64: 
65: (b) THE CONTROLS THAT REDDENED ARE ACCEPT-CELL COVERAGE BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT CONTROL DEFECTS.  sw08 halts / sw08 msg
66:     ctl are 4-byte writes to the HIGH half (+0x08), devsig is a 4-byte read of the LOW half (+0x04), rev pc ctl is a
67:     4-byte read of the HIGH half (+0x00); refusing that cell refuses the control's own access.  So CONTROL=FAIL under
68:     those three mutants is the controls doing a second job.  No mutant reddened a control through any other route.
69:     Weak spot disclosed: `devsig hi' wants 0x0, which a refused read also returns, so it cannot vary under acc4rhi --
70:     it is a device-reads-0 row, not a discriminating control; acc4 rhi and rev pc ctl carry that cell.
71: 
72: EQUIVALENCE, per the rule that a mutant that will not die is a result: return1 is the only survivor and it is the
73: predicted one, with its warrant named (memory_rw.c's #95 pre-zero); an edit to that warrant re-runs this measurement.
74: 
75: DENOMINATOR for the pass-2 closing question: cells swept -- refusal {1,2} x {R,W} each by a confined fall-through
76: (len1only, len2only, readonly, wronly) plus the whole fall-through (fallsw); accept {8W, 8R, 4W lo, 4W hi, 4R lo,
77: 4R hi} each by its single-cell growth mutant; the latch (nolatch, latchinv); the text (fmtswap); the dispositions
78: (revert, fault, exit0, return1).  NOT swept: address-conditioned fall-throughs (a goto keyed on relative_addr), which
79: reach the switch only at the labels a refused access happens to name -- owed as a pass-2 question, not yet measured.
80: *** CORRECTED 2026-09-13 (pass 2, codex): "each by a confined fall-through" overclaims -- len1only, len2only, readonly
81: and wronly each admit TWO refusal cells into the switch (a width's R and W, or a direction's 1 and 2), so no table-1
82: mutant is confined to ONE cell.  The single-cell forms (only1r, only2r, only1w, only2w) are measured in kill table 2.
83: And the NOT-SWEPT class above was then MEASURED LIVE by the pass-2 Opus seat: a decline narrowed to skip INTSTAT,
84: INTMASK or TIME passed this 40-row instrument 40/40 (opus_pass2_20260913/OPUS_REPORT.md) -- repaired in table 2. ***

