200: *** THE LATCH-KEYED ACCEPT SHRINK (the K-CLASS) AND ITS CLOSURE -- repair 13, and it is the reason this probe grew
201: from 157 rows to 188. ***
202: 
203: An accept guard grown with a conjunct on THIS FIX'S OWN LATCH -- `&& !(<cell> && (d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))' -- declines
204: SILENTLY at that cell once any refusal has happened, because the latch is exactly what suppresses the announce.  Three
205: instances were MEASURED at 157/157 with a guest loss on the 157-row instrument (closing pass 7, opus_close7_20260915/
206: OPUS_REPORT.md): K1 at INTMASK 4W, K2 at the REV 4-byte cell, K3 at CONTROL 8R.  The value rows at THOSE THREE
207: CELLS are measured with the latch CLEAR, so none of them could see it.
