VERDICT: 8 false or unsupported sentences

Here, **P** is [crime_width_probe.r17.py](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/final529r17_20260926/crime_width_probe.r17.py:2), and **A** is `regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/`, within `GXEMUL-SEC`.

I read P’s complete docstring and row construction, the CRIME handler and relevant memory serialization code, the cited reports, and the tables’ PRETABLE, POSTTABLE, available check outputs and raw logs. Historical scores were checked against their historical instruments. I ran no emulator and changed no file.

The eight sentences requiring correction are:

1. **P:15 — “Every access … one `step` at a time.”**  
   False. `<RUN>` sends `continue`, allowing free execution ([P:564–568](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/final529r17_20260926/crime_width_probe.r17.py:564)). The saved measurement explicitly records the free-running access: [table16 base log:152–161](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/table16_20260926/logs/probe_base.raw:152). The guest-instruction assertion is supported; the stepping qualification is not.

2. **P:166–175 — the nonzero-byte assertion, specifically “TIME 66-990.”**  
   False as an unconditional range. [Table4’s base log:77](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/killtable4_20260913/logs/probe_base.raw:77) records `time lb … (raw 0)`. [Close3’s report:186–194](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/opus_close3_20260913/OPUS_REPORT.md:186) explicitly rejects this range and records 42 zero-valued cells among 800. P:187–189 acknowledges that evidence, but the earlier assertion remains.

3. **P:247–248 — the host-diagnostic bucket’s “missing two are not named anywhere.”**  
   False. The cited [close7 report:115–117](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/opus_close7_20260915/OPUS_REPORT.md:115) enumerates all five members. The supposedly missing two are **CONTROL 4W and 8W at `0x0001`**. The same report also enumerates all ten equivalent members at lines 112–114.

4. **P:248–250 — repair13’s three-write count means both `0x0201` cells have a detecting row.**  
   False for repair13. Its frozen probe contains `sd 0x0001`, `sw 0x0001` and **only `sw 0x0201`**, followed by a count expecting three: [table11 probe:1211–1224](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/killtable11_20260916/crime_width_probe.table11.py:1211). The missing `sd 0x0201` was added in repair14, as P itself correctly explains at lines 277–279. Current construction includes it at [P:1512](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/final529r17_20260926/crime_width_probe.r17.py:1512), and the count expects **four**, at P:1550–1551.

5. **P:430–432 — “the 66-990 the first tick adds.”**  
   This independently repeats the unsupported range from finding 2. The contradicting recorded observation is again [table4 base log:77](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/killtable4_20260913/logs/probe_base.raw:77): zero. The stated inability of the coarse threshold to distinguish a narrow store can remain; its numerical premise needs correction. This is counted separately because the requested unit is sentences.

6. **P:449–452 — TIME’s upper word is unconditionally equivalent because “TIME is kept to 32 bits.”**  
   **Conditional, by source reading.** Accepted writes can populate the full register or its upper word: [dev_sgi_ip32.c:275–287](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_ip32.c:275). Truncation to 32 bits happens only inside `if (to_add >= 1)`: [lines 153–172](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_ip32.c:153). Initial, same-microsecond or backward-clock updates can have zero delta. The equivalence therefore requires that the upper word actually be zero at the refusal. This is a source-derived qualification, not a newly measured counterexample.

7. **P:453–454 — “every byte is seeded nonzero, so any selection shows.”**  
   False without specifying where the selected bits land. The tail serializes only the low `len` bytes: [memory.c:99–107](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/memory.c:99). A selection remaining above those bytes does not show. P:175–177 already expressly identifies `& 0xffff0000` as equivalent for these `lb`/`lh` observations. This conclusion follows from the source and the docstring’s own counterexample.

8. **P:482–483 — the listed CONTROL bits, including “the low nibbles,” are “written by no accepted row.”**  
   False for low-nibble bit 0. `ACCEPTS` writes `0x0001` and `0x0201` at both widths: [P:1088–1089](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/final529r17_20260926/crime_width_probe.r17.py:1088). The saved symbolic census confirms those writes in both latch states: [accepts_ctl_writes.out:4–20](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/crimewidthkill/opus_r15p2_20260926/accepts_ctl_writes.out:4). The outside-contract classification may remain, but “no accepted row” cannot justify it.

